## Files you do **not** bump for app version

- `package-lock.json` dependency `"version"` lines (npm packages)
- `.github/workflows/main.yml` — `node-version` / `java-version` are toolchain, not app version
- `android/settings.gradle` / `android/build.gradle` — React Native Gradle versions
- XML `<?xml version="1.0"?>` headers in drawables/mipmaps

---

## Recommended workflow (agent scope)

```bash
# 1. Set semver (updates package.json + package-lock.json)
npm version X.Y.Z --no-git-tag-version

# 2. Edit manually (same semver everywhere):
#    - app.json → expo.version + expo.runtimeVersion (unless user said OTA-only)
#    - android/app/build.gradle → versionName + versionCode (+1)
#    - android/.../strings.xml → expo_runtime_version

# 3. Verify
grep -r "X.Y.Z" app.json package.json android/app/build.gradle android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
grep versionCode android/app/build.gradle

# 4. Propose commit (user approves) — chore: bump version to X.Y.Z
```

### OTA-only bump (user must say so explicitly)

- **Do not** change `runtimeVersion`, `versionCode`, or iOS build number
- User runs `eas update` themselves when ready

### Out of scope for agents (user handles manually)

- `eas update`, `eas build`, Play Store / App Store submission
- `npx expo prebuild` (unless user explicitly asks)
- Post-bump deploy or release instructions in chat

