## Quick checklist (copy before release)

- [ ] `app.json` → `expo.version`
- [ ] `app.json` → `expo.runtimeVersion` (if binary changes)
- [ ] `package.json` → `version`
- [ ] `package-lock.json` → root `version` (via `npm version`)
- [ ] `android/app/build.gradle` → `versionName`
- [ ] `android/app/build.gradle` → `versionCode` (+1 for Play Store)
- [ ] `android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml` → `expo_runtime_version`
- [ ] `ios/.../Info.plist` (if `ios/` exists) → short version + build number
- [ ] Commit: `chore: bump version to X.Y.Z`

---

## Conventions for agents

- Bump **every file in the checklist** in one logical commit (`chore:` prefix).
- Never bump only `package.json` — Android and Expo OTA strings will drift.
- Increment Android **`versionCode`** on each version bump (keeps future Play uploads valid).
- Ask the user whether the bump is **OTA-only** or **includes `runtimeVersion`** before editing.
- **Do not** run or suggest `eas build`, `eas update`, Play Store steps, or prebuild unless the user asks.
- After the commit proposal, **stop** — user runs EAS when ready.
